Security maturity develops progressively as organizations strengthen their Azure security posture over time.

Typical maturity stages include:

* Basic security controls
* Identity protection
* Continuous monitoring
* Automated security responses
* Threat intelligence integration
* Proactive risk management

For example, an organization may initially implement Multi-Factor Authentication and RBAC before later adopting automated threat detection and continuous compliance monitoring.

A real-life use case is enterprises improving cybersecurity as their cloud footprint expands.

Security maturity reduces organizational exposure to cyber threats while improving regulatory compliance.
